<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Feb farm import value down 10.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Feb farm import value down 10.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Taiwan's agriculture imports in February was US$205.7 million, down 10.6 percent from US$230.0 million in February 1996, the Finance Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Grain and oilseed imports were the top agriculture items.</p>
<p>Taiwan traders attributed the fall in February import values to the long Chinese Lunar New Year holidays at mid-month and delays in shipment deliveries.</p>
<p>Shipment delays were caused by poor weather conditions in January and early February in U.S. areas where major grain export facilities are located.</p>
<p>February import tonnages were not available, but traders estimated 500,000 tonnes of corn and 155,000 tonnes of soybeans would have arrived at Taiwan ports during February.</p>
<p>Major grain import categories (in millions US$):</p>
<p>			     February 1997    February 1996</p>
<p> Wheat				  26.3		 31.1</p>
<p> Corn				   84.1		 88.0</p>
<p> Soybeans			     43.6		 57.3</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
